ctr: optional picture for the idle touch screen

While a game runs the touch screen only shows "Tap the Touch Screen to go
to the Retroarch menu" as plain text. When bottom_idle.png is found next
to bottom_menu.png (directory_bottom_assets), draw that picture instead,
so an injected title can show a Virtual Console style screen. It is also
drawn instead of the "Asset(s) not found" screen when bottom_menu.png is
missing.

An injected title always reads its touch screen pictures from the RomFS:
a bottom assets folder saved in the game's retroarch.cfg by an older build
no longer hides them.

Applies on top of 0003, to RetroArch v1.22.2 (RETROARCH_REF in versions.env).

--- a/frontend/drivers/platform_ctr.c
+++ b/frontend/drivers/platform_ctr.c
@@ -289,6 +289,13 @@
    if (!ctr_injected || !settings)
       return;
 
+   /* The touch screen pictures are in the RomFS: a folder saved in the
+    * game's retroarch.cfg by an older build must not hide them. */
+   if (     path_is_valid(CTR_INJECTED_BOTTOM)
+         || path_is_valid(CTR_INJECTED_ROOT "bottom_idle.png"))
+      configuration_set_string(settings,
+            settings->paths.directory_bottom_assets, CTR_INJECTED_ROOT);
+
    ctr_injected_bezel_overlay(overlay, sizeof(overlay));
    if (string_is_empty(overlay))
    {
